; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Recursive Fern
; CATEGORY: Fractals
; LEVEL:    Advanced
; TAGS:     recursion, fern, three recursive calls, nature
; SUMMARY:  Grows a curling fern frond with a procedure that calls itself three times.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   A fern frond is a stem with leaflets on both sides, and each
;   leaflet looks like a smaller frond. This program says exactly
;   that in Logo. The stem itself is a slightly shorter fern that
;   bends a little, which is why the whole frond curls over at the
;   top. Two fronds grow from one clump.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Try changing :bend, the 70 degree leaflet angle or
;   the sizes in the last lines.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * three recursive calls with different sizes and turns
;   * a :side input of 1 or -1 that flips the curl
;   * a recursion that shrinks by subtracting, not just by dividing
;   * keeping every call balanced so the turtle returns home
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Set :bend to 0 for a straight frond, or 10 for a tight curl.
;   * Change :scale to grow the same fern bigger or smaller.
;   * Change 0.5 to 0.6 for bushier leaflets.
;   * Make the youngest leaflets yellow-green.
; ============================================================

; FERN draws a frond of length :size. :side says which way it curls.
to fern :size :side
  if :size < 1 [stop]
  ; Color: darker on the big stems, brighter on the tiny tips.
  setpencolor (list 40 90 + 100 / :size 40)
  setpensize :size / 7
  ; :size counts "segments"; :scale turns that into turtle steps, so
  ; the shape of the fern and its size on screen are kept apart.
  forward :size * :scale
  ; Leaflet on one side, curling the opposite way
  right 70 * :side
  fern :size * 0.5 minus :side
  left 70 * :side
  forward :size * :scale
  ; Leaflet on the other side
  left 70 * :side
  fern :size * 0.5 :side
  right 70 * :side
  ; The rest of the stem is itself a fern, a bit shorter and bent.
  right :bend * :side
  fern :size - 1 :side
  left :bend * :side
  ; Walk back down so the caller finds the turtle where it left it.
  back 2 * :size * :scale
end

; FROND grows one fern from (x, y) leaning toward :heading.
to frond :x :y :heading :size :side
  penup setxy :x :y setheading :heading pendown
  fern :size :side
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [245 240 225]
make "bend 6
make "scale 1.7
frond -20 -285 -20 16 1
frond 20 -285 25 14 -1
